# TEACH Ticket System — environment variable reference
#
# Phase 2 (database foundation) does not include actual database
# credentials. Real values belong in a local, git-ignored environment file
# (e.g. .env, .env.local) or in managed deployment secrets — never in this
# file and never committed to source control.
#
# Rules for every future phase:
# - Document new variables here using their NAME and a safe placeholder only
#   (e.g. EXAMPLE_VARIABLE=replace-with-your-value) — never a real value.
# - Real credentials, tokens, keys, or connection strings must never be
#   committed to this repository under any filename.
#
# Neither variable below is required merely to build or preview the
# application — they are only read by explicit database commands
# (`npm run db:migrate`, `npm run db:seed`).

# Runtime/application PostgreSQL connection (future use).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:replace-with-your-value@host:5432/database

# Optional direct migration/seed connection. Useful when a provider
# distinguishes a pooled runtime connection from a direct migration
# connection. Migration and seed commands prefer this and fall back to
# DATABASE_URL when it is not set.
# DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL=postgresql://user:replace-with-your-value@host:5432/database
